---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";
---

<Base
  title={`Cognitive Neuroscience & Language | ${site.name}`}
  description="Cognitive neuroscience and language processing: Cortex 2026 MEG/EEG sentence decoding, EMNLP 2023 psycholinguistics, and first-author LLM evaluation (IJCNLP, Springer AICS)."
  path="/neuroimaging-ml/"
>
  <header class="page-header">
    <h1>Cognitive neuroscience and language processing</h1>
    <p>
      PhD at NeuroSpin under Prof. Stanislas Dehaene. Flagship output: a
      <em>Cortex</em> paper on hierarchical versus sequential computations during
      sentence reading (MEG and EEG, compared to an LSTM language model). Separate
      first-author work on grammatical agreement (EMNLP 2023, Singapore) and LLM evaluation
      papers.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="page-section" aria-labelledby="cortex-heading">
    <h2 id="cortex-heading"><em>Cortex</em> (2026)</h2>
    <p>
      First author on
      <em>Disentangling Hierarchical and Sequential Computations during Sentence Processing</em>
      (<em>Cortex</em>, Elsevier), with Stanislas Dehaene and Yair Lakretz.
      Twenty-two participants read sentences in a rapid serial visual presentation
      (RSVP) task while we recorded combined magnetoencephalography (MEG) and
      electroencephalography (EEG) at NeuroSpin and ICM, Paris.
    </p>
    <p>
      We manipulated structural (hierarchical) subject–verb agreement and local
      transition (sequential) agreement for grammatical number and animacy, and
      ran the same sentences through a two-layer long short-term memory (LSTM)
      language model. The main neural result: in human MEG/EEG, only the
      structural effect is decodable above chance; transition and congruity
      decoding stay at chance throughout the trial window. The model decodes all
      three effects.
    </p>
    <p class="text-link-row">
      <a href="/publications/#group-neuroimaging-sentence">Publication entry with figure →</a>
      ·
      <a
        href="https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0010945226000456"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >ScienceDirect</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section" aria-labelledby="phd-heading">
    <h2 id="phd-heading">PhD, NeuroSpin / Sorbonne University</h2>
    <p>
      Supervised by Prof. Stanislas Dehaene (Collège de France). Designed and ran
      neuroimaging experiments with EEG and MEG; additional intracranial work with
      collaborators is outside the <em>Cortex</em> paper above.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section" aria-labelledby="emnlp-heading">
    <h2 id="emnlp-heading">EMNLP 2023 (Singapore)</h2>
    <p>
      First author on a paper at EMNLP 2023 in Singapore (Empirical Methods in
      Natural Language Processing; top 14% of submissions): grammatical agreement
      in humans and language models. Co-authored with researchers from Meta AI and
      NeuroSpin. Completed alongside clinical machine learning work on intravascular
      biosignals.
    </p>
    <p>
      First-author language-model evaluation work at IJCNLP 2025 (personality
      traits in large language models) and Springer AICS 2025 (semantic
      violation detection in causal LMs). Figures and detail on the{" "}
      <a href="/publications/#domain-llm-evaluation">publications page</a>.
    </p>
    <p class="text-link-row">
      <a href="/publications/">All publications →</a>
      ·
      <a href="/">Home</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
